sequential multicast ->
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This is a message routing step that sends a copy of the same message to multiple
routes in a specific order.you can use parallel multicast in scenarios where you
need to perform multiple operations on the same message in parallel or
where the order of execution in important. it is used when one path dependent
on another path
-> Only after the first path is finished (successfully or with an error), the second branch starts

Note :  No configurations only we can change  sequential order
        Select the branch which you want to move up or down in the order.
        Use Move Up and Move Down to change the order.

  config : (General, Routing Sequence)
  General : Name

  Routing sequence
  Specify the sequence of execution of branches (TV):

  Sequence Order                Sequence Name
  1                              Branch 1
  2                              Branch 2
